# `transaction-type` Standalone Wire Specification

The codec maps a canonical transaction format name such as `Payment` to its
protocol `TxType` and writes that value as exactly two big-endian bytes. Decode
performs the reverse lookup and rejects unregistered values.

The input is a name, not a decimal type code. Registered values originate in
`transactions.macro`; reserved/deprecated enum slots that are not loaded into
`TxFormats` are not silently accepted. There is no field header in the
standalone payload.

